---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-presence-indicator</code> shows whether a person is available. Wrap their avatar in it:
  the dot sits on the avatar's bottom-end corner (bottom left in right-to-left pages) inside a ring
  of the surface color, and is sized to the avatar. Each <code>status</code> has its own shape as
  well as its own color: a filled circle (online), a crescent moon (away), a circle with a dash
  (busy) and a hollow ring (offline).
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem;'>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='online'><wc-avatar name='Ana Lima'></wc-avatar></wc-presence-indicator>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='away'><wc-avatar name='Grace Hopper'></wc-avatar></wc-presence-indicator>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='busy'><wc-avatar name='Ada Lovelace'></wc-avatar></wc-presence-indicator>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='offline'><wc-avatar name='Alan Turing'></wc-avatar></wc-presence-indicator>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Sizes</h3>
<p>
  The dot follows the avatar's <code>size</code>. Set <code>size</code> on the indicator to
  override it, or for a dot on its own.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem;'>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='online'><wc-avatar name='Ana Lima' size='sm'></wc-avatar></wc-presence-indicator>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='online'><wc-avatar name='Ana Lima' size='md'></wc-avatar></wc-presence-indicator>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='online'><wc-avatar name='Ana Lima' size='lg'></wc-avatar></wc-presence-indicator>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  The status is read as part of the person's name, not announced separately: the avatar above is
  named "Ana Lima, online". On its own, without an avatar, the dot is an image named by the
  status. <code>label</code> replaces the status text, such as "In a meeting". When the avatar
  sits on something other than the surface color, set <code>--presence-indicator-ring-color</code>
  to that background.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;'>
    <wc-presence-indicator status='busy' label='In a meeting'></wc-presence-indicator>
    <span>In a meeting</span>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Presence or status indicator</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>wc-presence-indicator</code>: a person's availability, attached to their avatar. The four
    statuses and their shapes are fixed and familiar from chat apps.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>wc-status-indicator</code>: the state of a thing (a service, a job, a device), a dot and a
    visible label next to its name, with the general intents. Use it too when a person's status is
    written out, such as "Away" in a profile.
  </li>
</ul>
